    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d469-a1">

                <pb facs="0906" n="782" sameAs="frus:frus1881/pg782"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 1 in No. 245.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Morgan to Señor
                            Mariscal</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1881-07-27"><hi rendition="#italic">July</hi> 27,
                        1881</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I am instructed to bring to the knowledge
                    of the Mexican Government the proceedings had by the commanding officer of the
                    United States troops at Fort Brown on the occasion of the much regretted death
                    of General Servando Canales.</p>
                <p>In conformity with said instructions I now inclose to your excellency copy of a
                    letter addressed to the Secretary of State by the Secretary of War, as also a
                    copy of a telegram addressed to the commanding officer of Fort Brown.</p>
                <p>I renew, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer><signed>P. H. MORGAN.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
